{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Theorem 2.1 of P. Keevash, \"Counting designs\" (arXiv:1504.02909), for (c,16)-typical graphs: there are c₀ > 0 and n₀ such that every graph G on n ≥ n₀ vertices with all degrees even and 3 | e(G) that is (c,16)-typical, with density d(G) > n^(-10^-7) and c ≤ c₀·d(G)^(10^6), has a triangle decomposition (KeevashTri.theorem_2_1). (c,h)-typical means |⋂_{x∈S} G(x)| = (1 ± |S|c)·d(G)^|S|·n for every vertex set S with |S| ≤ h; the paper's theorem assumes only c-typicality (h = 2, with the paper's tolerance), so the hypothesis here is stronger, and the paper's c-typical version is not covered. The density and typicality thresholds are the paper's (n^(-10^-7) and c₀·d^(10^6)); c₀ and n₀ are not explicit. The proof follows the paper's strategy (random algebraic template over F₂^a, Nibble, Cover, Hole, Completion), with every random greedy algorithm of the Completion replaced by a deterministic potential (pessimistic-estimator) argument. Earlier registered entries are imported as lake dependencies: the hypergraph matching nibble of Ehard–Glock–Joos (PALOMAR-2026-10-17-000004) and the Steiner triple system material of PALOMAR-2026-10-22-000017 v2. Mathlib does not contain this result.",
